0 56 637 [
[(The [poly] object is actually better suited to handle)]
[(polyphony, but you can set it to a single voice with the)]
[(first argument and ignore the left outlet output. The)]
[(second argument sets the object to "voice stealing" so new)]
[(pressed notes will replace previous ones that are still)]
[(pressed \050which can then get released without interfering\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 297 463 [
[(These simulate)]
[(MIDI messages)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 56 728 [
[(This patch shows how to make a monophonic synthesizer that)]
[(could be controlled from a MIDI keyboard. First, at top,)]
[(incoming MIDI notes are parsed via the [poly] object and)]
[(used to set pitch and trigger an attack/release envelope.)]
[(You can use your MIDI keyboard with [notein] to test it or)]
[(the messages below.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
